{
  // The `.mts` probes and verifiers, which the ROOT tsconfig does not see.
  //
  // WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. tsconfig.json's `include` lists `scripts/**/*.ts` —
  // NOT `.mts` — so all 14 `scripts/*.mts` were outside `tsc --noEmit`, and
  // `npm run lint` (`--ext .ts,.tsx`) did not read them either. That is exactly
  // where the last defect lived: probe-sdk-manager-launch.mts called
  // `spawnSdkSession` without preloading the ESM SDK, so it would have broken at
  // the moment production started working, silently. The fix for that was to make
  // the proof a required ARGUMENT — but a type gate only bites files a compiler
  // actually reads, and this one did not read the single file that had the bug.
  //
  // ⚠ `target` IS THE WHOLE POINT OF THE OVERRIDE. The root sets no `target`
  // (⇒ ES5) and these files use top-level `await`. Adding `scripts/**/*.mts` to
  // the root include instead produces 55 errors — measured 2026-08-02, and the
  // breakdown matters more than the total:
  //     51 × TS1378  top-level await          ┐
  //      1 × TS1432  top-level for-await      ├ all cleared by `target: es2022`
  //      1 × TS2802  MapIterator iteration    ┘
  //      2 × TS5097  literal `.ts` import extension
  //                  → cleared by `allowImportingTsExtensions` below
  // (55 is the TOTAL. An earlier version of this comment read "55 × TS1378 and
  // nothing else", which is wrong twice over — TS1378 is 51, and three other
  // codes are involved. A measured number written down wrong is worse than no
  // number: whoever re-runs this sees 51, concludes something changed, and stops
  // trusting the rest of the note.)
  // Everything else is inherited on purpose: same strictness, same
  // `moduleResolution: bundler` (extensionless relative imports, the way tsx runs
  // them), same paths.
  //
  // Run by `npm run typecheck`, and by scriptsTypecheck.test.ts so it cannot be
  // forgotten in a gate that only says `npx tsc --noEmit`.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "es2022",
    // These files are run by tsx, never emitted, and two of them import a
    // sibling by its literal `.ts` path (which tsx resolves fine). Legal only
    // with noEmit — inherited from the root — which is precisely this case.
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    // ⚠ THIS LINE IS A GUARD, NOT HOUSEKEEPING — DO NOT TIDY IT AWAY. With
    // `incremental: true` (inherited from the root) tsc writes
    // `tsconfig.scripts.tsbuildinfo` (~121KB) into the REPO ROOT, and the repo-
    // root fence (src/test/repoRootFence.ts) diffs a readdirSync baseline — it
    // does NOT read .gitignore — so the suite turns red. The nasty part is that
    // it hides locally after the first run (the file joins the next baseline),
    // so the symptom presents as "red on CI only", which is precisely when an
    // unexplained line gets deleted as noise. Measured 2026-08-02: flipping this
    // to true reproduces it ("appeared: tsconfig.scripts.tsbuildinfo").
    "incremental": false
  },
  "include": ["scripts/**/*.mts"]
}
